{title: Angels, from the Realms of Glory}
{artist: James Montgomery}
{genre: Christmas}
{style: Carol}
{flow: Opening}
{key: G}
{tempo: 100}
{time: 4/4}
{score: angels-from-the-realms-of-glory.abc}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]Angels, from the [C]realms of [G]glory
[G]Wing your flight o'er [D]all the [G]earth
[G]Ye who sang cre[C]ation's [G]story
[G]Now proclaim Mes[D]siah's [G]birth
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[C]Come and wor[G]ship, [D]come and wor[G]ship
[C]Worship [G]Christ, the [D]newborn [G]King
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]Shepherds, in the [C]field a[G]biding
[G]Watching o'er your [D]flocks by [G]night
[G]God with man is [C]now re[G]siding
[G]Yonder shines the [D]infant [G]light
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]Sages, leave your [C]contem[G]plations
[G]Brighter visions [D]beam a[G]far
[G]Seek the great De[C]sire of [G]nations
[G]Ye have seen His [D]natal [G]star
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[G]Saints, before the [C]altar [G]bending
[G]Watching long in [D]hope and [G]fear
[G]Suddenly the [C]Lord, de[G]scending
[G]In His temple [D]shall ap[G]pear
{end_of_verse}
